  "title": "osf work-tracker command group",
  "summary": "Adds an `osf work-tracker` command group with two subcommands: `ready` reads the single GitHub Project item marked Ready (via the existing GitHub adapter), and `report` writes a state plus a recap back to one item. A new `[work_tracker]` table in `osf.toml` (owner, project_number, optional status_field/skip_status) configures the adapter, and the general config loader now strips that table so it does not trip `deny_unknown_fields`. The change is a thin CLI shell over the pre-existing `work_tracker`, `github_work_tracker` and `config` modules.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
